  "body": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/2002 states that nested list items have a list owner (so, even if they’re not direct children of `<ul>`, etc.), but the HTML spec for `<li>` starts with: \r\n\r\n> The li element represents a list item. If its parent element is an ol, ul, or menu element, then the element is an item of the parent element's list, as defined for those elements. Otherwise, the list item has no defined list-related relationship to any other li element.\r\n\r\nShould “parent” be updated?",
